---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
const effectiveDate = "May 1, 2026";
const lastUpdated = "May 1, 2026";
---

<Base title="Editorial Policy | GoDoDaytona" subtitle="GoDoDaytona's editorial standards, independence policy, and guidelines for sponsored and featured content." cityBase="daytona">
  <div class="lgWrap">

    <nav class="lgBread" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/daytona/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
      <a href="/daytona/legal/">Legal</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
      <span>Editorial Policy</span>
    </nav>

    <span class="lgEyebrow">GoDoDaytona</span>
    <h1 class="lgTitle">Editorial Policy</h1>
    <div class="lgMeta">
      <span>Effective: {effectiveDate}</span>
      <span>Last Updated: {lastUpdated}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="lgDivider"></div>

    <div class="lgNotice">
      <p>Advertising funds this publication. It does not direct it. The policies below explain exactly where the line is — and how we protect it.</p>
    </div>

    <nav class="lgToc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p class="lgTocTitle">Contents</p>
      <ol class="lgTocList">
        <li><a href="#mission">1. Our Mission</a></li>
        <li><a href="#independence">2. Editorial Independence</a></li>
        <li><a href="#standards">3. Reporting Standards</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sponsored">4. Sponsored & Branded Content</a></li>
        <li><a href="#featured">"Today's Best," "Featured," and Curated Mentions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#newsletter">6. Newsletter Advertising</a></li>
        <li><a href="#corrections">7. Corrections & Updates</a></li>
        <li><a href="#conflicts">8. Conflicts of Interest</a></li>
        <li><a href="#community">9. Community-Submitted Content</a></li>
        <li><a href="#ai">10. Artificial Intelligence</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact">11. Contact the Editorial Team</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <div class="lgSection" id="mission">
      <h2>1. Our Mission</h2>
      <p>GoDoDaytona exists to serve the Daytona Beach and Volusia County community with accurate, useful, and engaging local coverage. We cover news, events, dining, guides, business spotlights, and community life through a place-based lens rooted in the people and neighborhoods that make this area worth knowing.</p>
      <p>Our obligation is to our readers first. Our advertising partners fund the operation; they do not direct it. Those two things must always be true simultaneously, and these policies explain how we keep them that way.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="independence">
      <h2>2. Editorial Independence</h2>
      <p>Advertising, sponsorship, and paid partnership relationships have no influence over our news coverage decisions. The people who sell advertising at GoDoDaytona do not make editorial decisions. Our editors decide what to cover, how to cover it, and what to publish based solely on newsworthiness, community relevance, and reader value.</p>
      <p>We do not accept payment — in any form, including advertising purchases, gifts, meals, event tickets, or business favors — in exchange for favorable editorial coverage. Advertising with GoDoDaytona does not generate editorial mentions, endorsements, or inclusions in independent editorial roundups.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="standards">
      <h2>3. Reporting Standards</h2>
      <p>All editorial content published on GoDoDaytona.com is reviewed by an editor before publication. Our editorial team strives to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Verify information with primary sources before publishing.</li>
        <li>Clearly distinguish between reported facts and editorial opinion or analysis.</li>
        <li>Attribute statements and claims to named sources where possible.</li>
        <li>Correct errors promptly and transparently.</li>
        <li>Represent the full diversity of the Daytona Beach community in our coverage.</li>
        <li>Avoid sensationalism and clickbait that misrepresents the content of a story.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="sponsored">
      <h2>4. Sponsored & Branded Content</h2>
      <p>GoDoDaytona publishes paid editorial-format content as part of our advertising product menu. These products include The Deep Dive (Feature Article) and The Local Spotlight (Mini Article). This type of content:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Is always labeled with "Sponsored," "Paid Partnership," "Presented by [Brand]," or an equivalent disclosure that is clearly visible before a reader encounters the substantive content.</li>
        <li>Is written in the GoDoDaytona editorial voice by our team, but is shaped around the advertiser's message, story, or offer.</li>
        <li>Is reviewed by our editorial team to meet the same factual accuracy standards as organic editorial content.</li>
        <li>Is never disguised as independent journalism or presented without disclosure.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Sponsored content is commercially motivated. The views, claims, and characterizations in sponsored content reflect the advertiser's business and messaging, not GoDoDaytona's independent editorial assessment of that business.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="featured">
      <h2>5. "Today's Best," "Featured," and Curated Mentions</h2>
      <p>GoDoDaytona publishes curated roundups, "Today's Best" selections, "Featured" business spotlights, and similar curated content across our website, newsletter, and social channels. These placements may arise from two distinct contexts:</p>
      <h3>Organically Selected</h3>
      <p>An editorial team member identifies a business, event, or experience as genuinely worth sharing with our audience — based on quality, timing, community relevance, or reader interest — with no commercial arrangement involved. These mentions represent the independent opinion of our editorial team and are not labeled as sponsored.</p>
      <h3>Partnership-Based Placements</h3>
      <p>A "Featured," "Today's Best," or curated mention that involves a paid commercial arrangement with the featured business. These placements are selected, scheduled, and produced under a contractual advertising agreement. They will be clearly labeled as "Sponsored," "Featured Partner," "Paid Placement," or with an equivalent disclosure.</p>
      <p><strong>The absence of a sponsorship label means the mention is editorial.</strong> The presence of any sponsorship label means a commercial relationship exists. We do not use sponsorship labels selectively or inconsistently.</p>
      <p>Paying for an advertising product with GoDoDaytona does not guarantee organic editorial coverage, inclusion in unlabeled roundups, or independent endorsement of any kind.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="newsletter">
      <h2>6. Newsletter Advertising</h2>
      <p>The GoDoDaytona morning newsletter contains clearly labeled advertising placements, including text ads (The Daily Mention), image banner ads (The Anchor, The Top Line, The High-Impact Showcase), and sponsored content links. All paid inclusions in the newsletter are visually separated from editorial content and labeled "Sponsored," "Presenting Partner," or "Premium Partner" as appropriate to the placement.</p>
      <p>Our editorial staff selects newsletter story coverage independently of which advertisers are running in a given issue.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="corrections">
      <h2>7. Corrections & Updates</h2>
      <p>We are committed to accuracy, and mistakes happen. When they do, we correct them as quickly as possible. Our corrections policy:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Factual errors in editorial content are corrected with a labeled "Correction" note appended to the article, including the date of correction and a brief description of what changed.</li>
        <li>Material errors that significantly change the meaning of a story may require a separate correction notice.</li>
        <li>We do not silently edit published articles to remove errors without notation.</li>
        <li>Corrections to sponsored content are coordinated with the advertiser and clearly noted.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To report an error, email <a href="mailto:hello@gododaytona.com">hello@gododaytona.com</a> with "Correction Request" in the subject line. Include a link to the article and a description of the error.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="conflicts">
      <h2>8. Conflicts of Interest</h2>
      <p>GoDoDaytona team members are required to disclose potential conflicts of interest to their editors before working on any story where such a conflict could affect — or appear to affect — their objectivity. Editors will reassign coverage, add a disclosure at the bottom of the published piece, or both, as the situation warrants.</p>
      <p>We do not accept gifts, complimentary meals, free event tickets, travel, or other items of value from businesses or individuals we cover editorially, except where such access is part of the standard reporting process (e.g., attending a public event or visiting a restaurant on assignment with full disclosure).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="community">
      <h2>9. Community-Submitted Content</h2>
      <p>We welcome tips, story ideas, event submissions, press releases, and letters from the Daytona Beach community. Submission does not guarantee publication. Submitted content may be edited for length, clarity, and style before publication.</p>
      <p>We do not publish content that is defamatory, discriminatory, factually unverifiable, or that advocates unlawful activity. Community-submitted content that is published will be attributed to the submitter unless anonymity is requested and granted.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="ai">
      <h2>10. Artificial Intelligence</h2>
      <p>GoDoDaytona may use AI-assisted tools for research support, first-draft generation, data analysis, and content summarization as part of our editorial workflow. Our policy:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>All content published under GoDoDaytona bylines is reviewed, edited, and approved by a human editor before publication.</li>
        <li>AI tools do not replace editorial judgment, source verification, or community accountability.</li>
        <li>We do not publish AI-generated content without meaningful human review.</li>
        <li>Where AI tools are used in a material way in producing a specific story, we may note that in the article.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="contact">
      <h2>11. Contact the Editorial Team</h2>
      <p>For editorial questions, corrections, story tips, and feedback:</p>
      <p><strong>GoDoDaytona Editorial</strong><br><a href="mailto:hello@gododaytona.com">hello@gododaytona.com</a></p>
      <p>For advertising and sponsorship inquiries, see our <a href="/daytona/advertise/">Advertise</a> page or email <a href="mailto:ads@godocity.com">ads@godocity.com</a>.</p>
    </div>

  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .lgWrap { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 56px 2rem 96px; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .lgWrap { padding: 40px 1.25rem 72px; } }
  .lgBread { font-size: 13px; color: #888; margin-bottom: 32px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .lgBread a { color: var(--brand1, #0077be); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }
  .lgBread a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .lgBread span[aria-hidden] { color: #ccc; }
  .lgEyebrow { display: block; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--brand1, #0077be); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .lgTitle { font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 42px); font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: -0.025em; color: #111; margin: 0 0 16px; line-height: 1.1; }
  .lgMeta { font-size: 13px; color: #888; margin-bottom: 28px; display: flex; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .lgDivider { height: 1px; background: #e5e7eb; margin: 0 0 32px; }
  .lgNotice { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand1, #0077be) 6%, white); border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand1, #0077be) 20%, transparent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .lgNotice p { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: #333; }
  .lgToc { background: #f9f9fb; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px 24px; margin-bottom: 52px; }
  .lgTocTitle { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #888; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .lgTocList { list-style: decimal; padding-left: 18px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 7px; }
  .lgTocList a { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; color: #333; text-decoration: none; }
  .lgTocList a:hover { color: var(--brand1, #0077be); text-decoration: underline; }
  .lgSection { margin-bottom: 52px; }
  .lgSection h2 { font-size: clamp(17px, 2.5vw, 21px); font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: #111; margin: 0 0 18px; padding-bottom: 10px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--brand1, #0077be); }
  .lgSection h3 { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 800; color: #111; margin: 22px 0 8px; }
  .lgSection p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.78; color: #444; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .lgSection p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .lgSection ul, .lgSection ol { padding-left: 22px; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .lgSection li { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.72; color: #444; margin-bottom: 7px; }
  .lgSection a { color: var(--brand1, #0077be); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .lgSection strong { color: #111; }
  @media print { .lgWrap { padding: 0; } .lgBread { display: none; } }
</style>
